commit c44c7bc62d4ef341951ef1f3c79e2ec0e1449a29
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Fri Jul 10 16:01:23 2026 -0700

    Fix WriteMLMF: refinement ratio computed from bigEnd instead of length (#5558)
    
    Using bigEnd (last index) to compute refinement ratio gives wrong values
    for small coarse domains: (r*Nc-1)/(Nc-1) equals r only when Nc > r. For
    example, a 2-cell coarse domain refined by 2 yields 3/1=3 instead of 2.
    Use length(d) instead, matching the reader's refRatioVect computation.

