    The function is not used anywhere and it contains an undefined behavior
    of using std::isdigit on signed char.

Src/Base/AMReX_Utility.H
Src/Base/AMReX_Utility.cpp

commit 458129e1e26ffbbd88dc8bd855be4e325e8818f9
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Wed Jul 1 15:18:25 2026 -0700

    TimeIntegrator::integrate: fix swap guard for start_step != 0 (#5536)
    
    The swap guard used `m_step_number > 0`, but the loop counter starts
    from `start_step`. When `start_step > 0` (e.g. restarting from a
    checkpoint), the first iteration would incorrectly swap S_old/S_new
    before advancing, causing advance() to read from the uninitialized S_new
    buffer instead of the actual initial condition in S_old. Change the
    guard to `m_step_number > start_step` so the first step of each
    integrate() call never swaps, matching the intent.

Src/Base/AMReX_TimeIntegrator.H

commit a9dc2b7b650afb7a3cc17ea09c69923b4ec13d10
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Wed Jul 1 14:37:26 2026 -0700

    Fix UB in ParmParse (#5535)
    
    The behavior of the functions in cctype is undefined if the argument's
    int value is negative. To use these functions safely with char's, we
    must cast the argument to unsigned char.

