commit 6e39ba58c745dd45c94d9a4760a04a800370a1a6
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Wed Jul 1 13:22:52 2026 -0700

    Make memory management safer in Fortran APIs (#5487)
    
    Add destroy() calls before overwriting C++ pointers in _build, _assign,
    _install, _clone, and _move methods across the Fortran interfaces. The
    destroy functions are no-ops when no C++ object is owned, so they are
    safe to call on freshly constructed or already-destroyed objects.
    
    This guards against leaks if users call _build or similar methods
    multiple times without an intervening _destroy.

