commit af3a54ae42d7d8956e21f4fd192f71833f12cb45
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Thu Jun 4 11:30:00 2026 -0700

    C++20: Remove artificial member-template parameters (#5468)
    
    Replace member function templates whose template parameters exist solely
    to mirror enclosing class-template parameters with constrained
    non-template members. For the few cases where real call-time template
    parameters remain alongside artificial ones, drop only the artificial
    parameters.
    
    The pattern before C++20 required a dummy template parameter (e.g.,
    template<int MM=NRows>) just to use std::enable_if_t. C++20 allows
    trailing requires on non-template members, making these helpers
    unnecessary.
    
    Co-Authored-By: deepseek-v4-pro[1m]

