commit 7c6df9a0cd8fe9a9236851af5f6d25c840aaee6d
Author: Jon Rood <jon.rood@nrel.gov>
Date:   Mon Apr 27 13:04:33 2026 -0600

    Call HYPRE_DeviceInitialize after HYPRE_Init if using GPUs (#5336)
    
    Without this, I was experiencing errors during init on a machine where
    MPI ranks can see multiple GPUs:
    ```
    CUDA ERROR (code = 1, invalid argument) at /whatever/hypre/src/utilities/memory.c:136
    ```
    
    Setting `export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` was able to avoid the error, but
    the actual fix seems to be to include the call to
    `HYPRE_DeviceInitialize()` after `HYPRE_Init()` when using GPUs.
    
    I can verify this solves the error I was seeing when using hypre with
    AMReX in AMR-Wind.

