commit 3c7601fb7f54d1ee1bce3e15a7e68e2f1abc5b0a
Author: Alexander Sinn <64009254+AlexanderSinn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Apr 15 03:42:54 2026 +0200

    Align Arena allocations to 256 bytes (#5278)
    
    ## Summary
    
    This PR increases the alignment of Arena allocations from 16 to 256
    bytes. This gives a small speedup when running on GPU.
    In this test the alignment affects only the particle data, while the
    field elements are only 8-byte aligned due to there being no padding for
    the 2D arrays.
    ```
    alignment: runtime in seconds of 3 runs
    512: 8.443, 8.461, 8.444
    256: 8.449, 8.459, 8.446
    128: 8.473, 8.466, 8.491
    64:  8.506, 8.508, 8.511
    32:  8.49,  8.491, 8.483
    16:  8.491, 8.489, 8.486
    8:   misaligned address !!!
    ```
    This could also help with SIMD on CPU
    
    ## Additional background
    
    It was not clear from the documentation what the alignment of memory
    allocated by hipMalloc is. I assume it is 256, the same as cudaMalloc.

