commit 42b18e9a4c3fe50bae43c6168e0661b3776575fb
Author: Axel Huebl <axelhuebl@lbl.gov>
Date:   Sun Apr 5 19:48:22 2026 -0700

    Fix `PolymorphicArenaWrapper` Use-After-Free (#5270)
    
    ## Summary
    
    - [x] Fix `PolymorphicArenaWrapper` use-after-free on `Arena`
    destruction
    
    `PolymorphicArenaWrapper` caches a raw `Arena*` that becomes dangling
    after `Arena::Finalize()` deletes the `CArena`. Unlike the
    non-polymorphic wrappers (`ArenaWrapper`, `DeviceArenaWrapper`, ...)
    which call getter functions that fall back to `The_Null_Arena()`, the
    polymorphic variant bypassed this safety net.
    
    Expose the existing file-static `initialized` flag via
    `Arena::IsInitialized()` and check it in
    `PolymorphicArenaWrapper::arena()`. When arenas have been torn down, the
    wrapper now falls back to `The_Arena()` -> `The_Null_Arena()`, whose
    `free()` is a no-op.
    
    ## Additional background
    
    - [x] Test: A `PODVector` backed by `PolymorphicArenaAllocator` that
    outlives `amrex::Finalize()` currently segfaults on GPU builds, because
    the allocator holds a dangling raw `Arena*` after `Finalize` deletes the
    `CArena`. This test captures the bug.
    
    Same happens for more complex types, like `ParticleContainer`. See,
    e.g.,: https://github.com/BLAST-ImpactX/impactx/pull/1383
    
    Related to https://github.com/AMReX-Codes/pyamrex/issues/81
    
    ## Checklist
    
    The proposed changes:
    - [x] fix a bug or incorrect behavior in AMReX
    - [ ] add new capabilities to AMReX
    - [ ] changes answers in the test suite to more than roundoff level
    - [ ] are likely to significantly affect the results of downstream AMReX
    users
    - [ ] include documentation in the code and/or rst files, if appropriate
    
