commit a22630c87bb4c44bde2ba3ed4a772421ce39f126
Author: Olivier Desjardins <olivier.desjardins@cornell.edu>
Date:   Wed Mar 11 16:00:58 2026 -0400

    Fix hidden direction support for multilevel composite solves (#5141)
    
    ## Summary
    
    AMRRefRatio stored a scalar int that was promoted to isotropic IntVect
    in inter-level operations (average_down, interpolation, reflux, boundary
    setup). With hidden direction and anisotropic refinement ratios (e.g.,
    2,2,1 for nz=1), this caused incorrect coarsening/interpolation in the
    hidden dimension.
    Changes:
    - Fix OOB access in m_amr_ref_ratio computation for hidden_direction=0
    - Add AMRRefRatioVect() helper returning IntVect with 1 in hidden dir
    - Use AMRRefRatioVect in all inter-level operations that need IntVect
    - Fix coarsenable assert to use anisotropic ratio
    - Modified assertion in define() that was preventing multilevel + hidden
    direction
    
    ## Additional background
    
    [Discussion
    here](https://github.com/AMReX-Codes/amrex/discussions/5140#discussion-9601195)

