commit f9ad2c62584fac5fd502011d93689b6680cdffc8
Author: Alexander Sinn <64009254+AlexanderSinn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 9 21:24:41 2025 +0200

    Improve usability of amrex::Gpu::Buffer (#4697)
    
    ## Summary
    
    This PR expands the capabilities of `amrex::Gpu::Buffer<T>` so that it
    can be first default constructed, then modified by the CPU, and lastly
    copied over to the GPU, instead of everything happening in the
    constructor.
    
    Example:
    ```C++
    amrex::Gpu::Buffer<int> buf;
    
    buf.resize(n);
    
    for (int i=0; i<n; ++i) {
        buf[i] = i*i;
    }
    
    buf.copyToDeviceAsync();
    
    int * ptr = buf.data();
    // Use ptr inside ParallelFor
    
    // optional:
    // Change values of ptr inside ParallelFor
    buf.copyToHost();
    // Use buf.hostData() or buf[] on the CPU
    ```
    
    ## Additional background
    
    Follow-up to discussion in
    https://github.com/AMReX-Codes/amrex/pull/4640

