commit c7d93bae43e1259a40b13e905918af24d6b8f03e
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Tue Sep 30 10:15:36 2025 -0700

    EB: Fix corner case (#4687)
    
    When the EB cuts off a tiny corner, we may encounter situations where
    five faces have an aperture of one and the remaining face with an
    aperture of almost one. In such cases, roundoff errors can significantly
    affect the computation of the normal and the boundary centroid. This PR
    addresses the issue by treating faces that are only minimally cut as
    regular faces.

