commit d62e94ba7413cf7fa7ef4f72fc22181d93220177
Author: Alexander Sinn <64009254+AlexanderSinn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Sep 22 20:32:26 2025 +0200

    Add range-based for and ND to BoxIterator (#4668)
    
    ## Summary
    
    This PR extends BoxIterator to be n-dimensional. Additionally, it now
    supports a range-based for loops. The hope is that this can be useful to
    reduce the reliance on ifdefs/macros to write loops over boxes that run
    on CPUs, though so far I haven't found that many places where this can
    be used.
    ```C++
    Box b;
    ...
    for (IntVect iv : b.iterator()) {
        // do operations involving iv
    }
    ```
    Note that while regular iteration of the range-based version is
    reasonably performant,
    it is not compatible with `omp parallel for` or simd autovectorization.
    
    ## Additional background
    
    The range-based version produces good assembly when compiling with -O3,
    having minimal instructions in the innermost loop.
    https://godbolt.org/z/MTcM8Ysaq
    ```C++
    void g (const IntVect&);
    
    void test (Box bx) {
        for (auto iv : bx.iterator()) {
            g(iv);
        }
    }
    ```
    ```assembly
            ...
    .L3:
            mov     ebx, DWORD PTR [rsp+8]
    .L4:
            mov     r15d, r13d
    .L6:
            mov     DWORD PTR [rsp+16], r15d
            lea     rdi, [rsp+16]
            add     r15d, 1
            mov     DWORD PTR [rsp+20], ebx
            mov     DWORD PTR [rsp+24], ebp
            call    "g(IntVectND<3> const&)"
            cmp     r15d, r12d
            jle     .L6
            add     ebx, 1
            cmp     r14d, ebx
            jge     .L4
            cmp     ebp, DWORD PTR [rsp+12]
            je      .L13
            add     ebp, 1
            jmp     .L3
            ...
    ```
    
    ## Checklist
    
    The proposed changes:
    - [ ] fix a bug or incorrect behavior in AMReX
    - [x] add new capabilities to AMReX
    - [ ] changes answers in the test suite to more than roundoff level
    - [ ] are likely to significantly affect the results of downstream AMReX
    users
    - [ ] include documentation in the code and/or rst files, if appropriate

