Author: Alexander Sinn <64009254+AlexanderSinn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Sep 16 16:39:41 2025 +0200

    Use `p.id().is_valid()` consistently (#4635)
    
    ## Summary
    
    This PR applies further cleaning to particles.
    
    The largest change is the replacement of all numeric id comparisons with
    `id().is_valid()` and `id().make_invlid()`. Previously, `id() > 0`,
    `id() < 0`, `id() < 1` and `id() <= 0` with `id() = - id()` were used,
    making the treatment of id == 0 inconsistent (particle ids start at 1
    because of this).
    
    Both `ptd.m_aos[i]` and `make_particle<ConstParticleType>{}(ptd, ip);`
    were replaced with `ptd[i]` which is more concise and works with PureSoA
    particles.
    
    The PureSoA specialization of numParticlesOutOfRange was removed because
    the other version also works with PureSoA particles.
    
    ## Additional background
    
    ## Checklist
    
    The proposed changes:
    - [x] fix a bug or incorrect behavior in AMReX
    - [ ] add new capabilities to AMReX
    - [ ] changes answers in the test suite to more than roundoff level
    - [ ] are likely to significantly affect the results of downstream AMReX
    users
    - [ ] include documentation in the code and/or rst files, if appropriate

