commit 2cf53a64f2fed9687a162993b4b1bf817a9904db
Author: Alexander Sinn <64009254+AlexanderSinn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu May 8 18:45:49 2025 +0200

    CArena free unused memory before allocate (#4451)
    
    ## Summary
    
    In specific special cases, an application may ask for chunks of memory
    with slightly increasing size. If these do not fit into the existing
    space of the arena, a new chunk of system memory has to be allocated
    every time. The old chunks that are slightly too small to be reused
    could accumulate and consume a lot of memory and would never get freed
    with the default release threshold of max long. This PR adds a check to
    free unused system memory before allocating new memory, while still
    keeping the total amount of memory the same to avoid excessive system
    allocations and frees.
    
    ## Additional background
    
    The fix from #4044 is reimplemented differently in the PR so that
    freeUnused_protected can be called.

