commit 1548946a8b36fe2313f6fa45ee3eaabb53a2635e
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Sat Jan 11 17:37:15 2025 -0800

    std::clamp -> amrex::Clamp (#4292)
    
    std::clamp is a constexpr function, and it is supposed to work in device
    code. However, std::clamp in gcc 14 seems to be incompatible with clang.
    This is causing clang based HIP compiler to fail on systems using gcc 14
    libstd as reported by multiple users. Here we work around the issue by
    using amrex::Clamp instead.

