Author: Andrew Myers <atmyers@lbl.gov>
Date:   Wed Nov 20 16:36:44 2024 -0800

    Add portable implementation of random numbers drawn from the Gamma distribution. (#4239)
    
    This adds support for drawing random numbers from the [Gamma
    distribution](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma_distribution) on CPUs
    and GPUs. The CPU version is thread-safe and calls the STL
    implementation, while the GPU version is implemented in terms of
    `amrex::Random` and `amrex::RandomNormal.`
    
    This figure shows some sample histograms for a few choices of the
    `alpha` and `beta` parameters.
    
    ![hist](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6ca0097b-1de3-45ad-9195-a4b6a6b7f5a2)
    
