Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Tue Jul 23 09:34:29 2024 -0700

    Nodal Solver: Use multi-color Gauss-Seidel on GPU (#4043)
    
    Because the nodal solver's Gauss-Seidel smoother is not thread safe on
    GPU, we have been using Jacobi. But recently an amr-wind test shows that
    the Jacobi smoother is not stable for some hard problems. Using a
    multi-color (4 in 2d and 8 in 3d) Gauss-Seidel smoother appears to work
    well.

