commit 1959b1f7026f69d352bc6a025380881578fe92ee
Author: Luca Fedeli <luca.fedeli@cea.fr>
Date:   Wed Feb 21 21:35:25 2024 +0100

    Fix bug in AMREX_ASSUME (#3773)
    
    ## Summary
    
    This PR fixes a couple of  bugs in `AMREX_ASSUME` :
    
    - If `nvcc` is used with `gcc/g++` as the host compiler we have to use
    `__builtin_assume(ASSUMPTION)` in device code and `if (ASSUMPTION) {}
    else { __builtin_unreachable(); }` in host code. Therefore we need to
    add `if defined(__CUDA_ARCH__)`
    
    - Even if `__builtin_assume` appears in the CUDA 11.1 documentation,
    tests carried out with the Compiler Explorer show that we actually need
    at least CUDA 11.2 .

