    CMake Tests Setup (#3244)
    
    Previously most of the tests even if compiled with MPI were run on only
    one process because they did not specify the number of tasks explicitly
    in their setup. For the three tests that did specify, they were run
    twice during CI, first on a single process and then on two processes,
    due to the setup in Tests/CMakeLists.txt. The setup was similar for
    OpenMP.
    
    This has changed. For tests compiled with OMP, they are run with two OMP
    threads, otherwise they are run with two MPI processes if they are built
    with MPI. This should make the CI tests faster.

