commit a30cc5fd3213bb8118510f252fa3f5ad0028525e
Author: Axel Huebl <axelhuebl@lbl.gov>
Date:   Thu Jan 12 08:44:13 2023 -0800

    SinCos: AppleClang Fix (#3094)
    
    ## Summary
    
    I noticed that in some situations, e.g., when building Python sources
    that include Python headers, `_GNU_SOURCE` is sometimes defined. This
    can confuse AppleClang builds of AMReX:
    ```
    error: no member named 'sincos' in the global namespace; did you mean '__sincos'?
        ::sincos(x, &r.first, &r.second);
    ```
    
    Adding the respective guard here should allow GCC builds on macOS but
    ignore the GCC-ism when building with AppleClang.
    
    Follow-up to  #3008
    
    ## Additional background
    
    First seen in pyAMReX the other week.
    Avoided with restructured includes, but ultimately a defect that CPython
    headers pull in.
    
    Seen again today by @RTSandberg

Src/Base/AMReX_Math.H

