commit 2e0b2b463306bc8c371b38e4e3125a8ed86698e3
Author: Weiqun Zhang <weiqunzhang@lbl.gov>
Date:   Thu Jan 5 12:18:47 2023 -0800

    New knapsack function to reduce the cost of data movement in load balancing (#3079)
    
    This adds a new function DistributionMapping::KnapSackProcessorMap that
    makes a new DistributionMapping given an old DistributionMapping, a
    vector of weights and a parameter affecting the amount of the data
    movement that would be needed for switching from the old to the new
    DistributionMapping.
    
    In this new knapsack function, some boxes will be kept on the current
    processes and the knapsack algorithm is applied to the rest of the
    boxes. This may generate a less optimal distribution. However, the new
    DistributionMapping is more similar to the old one, thus reducing the
    cost of data movement during load balancing.

